    "sourceDescription": "Dr. King'ori sits with Ambassador Brigadier general Dr. Wallace W. Williams, the honorary consul general for the Caribbean islands of Antigua and Barbuda to the federal republic of Nigeria, a military officer attaining the rank of Brigadier general for this interesting conversation that weaves through the world of a diplomat and probably the best explanation to the single parents boom.\n#GrinContent\nhttps://twitter.com/Dr_Kingori\n\nhttps://www.facebook.com/KingoriDr\n\n\nCHAPTERS\n\n0:00       Intro\n\n3:08       Inside the world of a diplomat\n\n10:56     The complexity of diplomatic language \n\n14:24     The idea of a cease fire and how it works\n\n17:13      The Geneva convention\n\n20:10      Ways to know whether the cease fire is a\n                trick or it is genuine\n\n24:07      War strategies\n\n26:27      Winning the war and the prize attached\n                  to it\n\n28:32       Difference between acts of war and\n                  provocation\n\n31:52       Understanding how diplomacy is related\n                   to spying\n\n35:58       Effects of diplomacy to a nation\n\n37:25       The depth of gestures in diplomacy\n\n39:41        What it takes for a country to join the \n                    union of other countries\n\n43:48       Ways of getting foreign citizenship by\n                   investment\n\n49:53        Dual citizenship,politics and swearing\n                    allegiance\n\n53:03        Marriage advice for young people\n\n56:01        Impact of strict positive discipline on\n                   children\n\n58:07        How inheritance interferes with the\n                   mindset of young people\n\n1:00:13      Being an all round parent\n\n1:01:07      Know why you want to marry\n\n1:02:42      Why most men die before their wives\n\n1:04:57      Marriage as a partnership where both\n                     parties benefit\n\n1:09:36       Being deliberate on your reasons for\n                     marriage and expectations\n\n1:12:39        Why arranged marriages succeed more\n\n1:13:38        Equal in value but different in\n                       responsibility\n\n1:17:41        How poor parenting has contributed to\n                      misleading decisions\n\n1:18:31       Equip children with survival skills\n\n1:22:06       The African agenda\n\n1:24:21       How inherited western cultures have \n                       affected Africans, their culture and it's\n                      Leadership\n\n1:30:29        Outro",
